STARVATION SPOILERS:

You should almost never die of starvation if you play correctly.  Eat
everything that is edible.  Never eat your food rations except in an
emergency.  Play until you get weak.  Then engrave Elbereth and stand over it
until you faint.  After fainting, pray.  You will be filled.

Try to eat at least one or two corpses before praying again.  This works
consistently for low-level players.  After you gain more experience levels
food is not so much of a problem.  Never pray unless you are already fainting.
Never pray immediately after praying.  If you are in trouble (praying doesn't
work) then eat one of the food rations you've been saving.

I stash food rations in chests every other level, so if I ever get in trouble
and I'm out of food, I know where to find it.  Food becomes fairly abundant
later on, though.

Only wear your rings briefly when you need their effects.  Rings increase your
rate of food usage while you are wearing them, especially regeneration.  Also,
teleporting uses a tremendous amount of food.  Getting sick and vomitting also
uses up extra food.
